 agents for psoriasis. A systematic review.</article-title> <source>J Rheumatol</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>33</volume>:<fpage>1442</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16724368</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mulrow</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Haynes</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Systematic reviews: synthesis of best evidence for clinical decisions.</article-title> <source>Ann Intern Med</source> <year>1997</year>;<volume>126</volume>:<fpage>376</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9054282</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thalheimer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>How to calculate effect sizes from published research articles: a simplified methodology.</article-title> <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.work-learning.com/effect_sizes.htm">http://www.work-learning.com/effect_sizes.htm</ext-link> (accessed 5 May 2008).</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Gladman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Helliwell</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Marchesoni</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mease</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mielants</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Classification criteria for psoriatic arthritis: development of new criteria from a large international study.</article-title> <source>Arthritis Rheum</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>54</volume>:<fpage>2665</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16871531</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gladman</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Mease</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Strand</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Healy</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Helliwell</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Consensus on a core set of domains for psoriatic arthritis.</article-title> <source>J Rheumatol</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>34</volume>:<fpage>1167</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17477480</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bond</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Farewell</surname><given-names>VT</given-names></name><name><surname>Schentag</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Gladman</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Predictors for radiological damage in psoriatic arthritis: results from a single centre.</article-title> <source>Ann Rheum Dis</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>66</volume>:<fpage>370</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16916855</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fransen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>